      "text": "To solve the expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\), we first need to identify the pattern and find the total number of terms in the sequence.\n\nThe sequence alternates between positive and negative terms. Let's list the first few terms to identify the pattern:\n\\[1, -4, 7, -10, 13, -16, \\ldots, 55.\\]\n\nThe sequence includes positive terms and negative terms. We can split the sequence into two separate sums: one for the positive terms and one for the negative terms.\n\nLet's first consider the positive terms:\n\\[1, 7, 13, 19, 25, 31, 37, 43, 49.\\]\n\nThis is an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and common difference \\(d = 6\\). To find the number of terms in this sequence, we use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:\n\\[a_n = a + (n-1)d.\\]\nWe set \\(a_n = 49\\) and solve for \\(n\\):\n\\[49 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 6,\\]\n\\[49 = 1 + 6n - 6,\\]\n\\[49 = 6n - 5,\\]\n\\[54 = 6n,\\]\n\\[n = 9.\\]\nSo, there are 9 positive terms.\n\nNext, let's consider the negative terms:\n\\[-4, -10, -16, -22, -28, -34, -40, -46.\\]\n\nThis is also an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a = -4\\) and common difference \\(d = -6\\). To find the number of terms in this sequence, we use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:\n\\[a_n = a + (n-1)d.\\]\nWe set \\(a_n = -52\\) and solve for \\(n\\):\n\\[-52 = -4 + (n-1) \\cdot (-6),\\]\n\\[-52 = -4 - 6n + 6,\\]\n\\[-52 = 2 - 6n,\\]\n\\[-54 = -6n,\\]\n\\[n = 9.\\]\nSo, there are also 9 negative terms.\n\nThe total number of terms in the sequence is \\(9 + 9 = 18\\). The sum of the positive terms is:\n\\[1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + 25 + 31 + 37 + 43 + 49 = \\sum_{k=0}^{8} (1 + 6k) = 9 \\cdot 1 + 6 \\sum_{k=0}^{8} k = 9 + 6 \\cdot \\frac{8 \\cdot 9}{2} = 9 + 6 \\cdot 36 = 9 + 216 = 225.\\]\n\nThe sum of the negative terms is:\n\\[-4 - 10 - 16 - 22 - 28 - 34 - 40 - 46 = -\\sum_{k=0}^{7} (4 + 6k) = -9 \\cdot 4 - 6 \\sum_{k=0}^{7} k = -36 - 6 \\cdot \\frac{7 \\cdot 8}{2} = -36 - 6 \\cdot 28 = -36 - 168 = -204.\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the entire expression is:\n\\[225 - 204 = 21.\\]\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\\boxed{21}.\\]",
